<http://data.silknow.org/event/f7816513-fdb7-317f-9000-c725e09a08ef>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "The knives were made in England by John or Joseph Jencks.  The embroidery design is identical to that on a purse and pincushion, T.52-1954, and all three may have been made as a set.  Bequeathed by Sir Frederick Richmond, Bart, in 1954, along with a collection of 17th century embroidery and accessories."@en ;
